n voters in late polls, or Stout's own opposition research gains traction, could push this toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Texas's 23rd is an open Republican-held border district after Tony Gonzales's resignation, with a partisan lean of about seven points toward the GOP. Republicans nominated gun-content creator Brandon Herrera, whose history of Nazi-related jokes and crude remarks has drawn national coverage, while House Speaker Mike Johnson has still backed him. Democrat Katy Padilla Stout has trailed in fundraising and faces her own negative stories.\n\nMost expert ratings call the race Likely or Lean Republican, though a couple put it closer. The only public poll, from a Democratic-leaning firm in March, showed a two-point Republican lead. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 40 percent chance. The forecast expects a narrow Republican win of about three points, with meaningful uncertainty given the nominee-driven dynamics.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}]}